1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,260
One dream,

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:08,260
one wish If you want it,
gotta go over the top!

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,680
Setting sail and heading for the unknown.

4
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,380
Cutting through the
winds and waves as I go.

5
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,437
Gotta keep it up, never stopping, no.

6
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,837
Cause I'm aiming to get there first, yeah.

7
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:41,417
It's all or nothing, no time to worry.

8
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,160
Do it later, right now I'm living free.

9
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:51,477
When your foes look like
they will overwhelm you.

10
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:56,400
It means your heart's saying
this is what you can't do.

11
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:59,537
Despite all that to run is not an option.

12
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:01,577
Once they're closed, I
feel the satisfaction.

13
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:03,937
You think I'm rude,
here's my appreciation.

14
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,040
When things are getting
tough, just gotta smile.

15
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:12,317
If you are going on your way.

16
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,577
And you're looking for
a fresh, brand new day.

17
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,737
Then make sure your only
thought you have is.

18
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:19,300
Yes, I can.

19
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:22,057
As you're on your way.

20
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,337
Marked maps will be made.

21
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:27,197
Yes, with every step that you will take.

22
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,397
Just look at all you've been through.

23
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:32,137
Look ahead to new horizons.

24
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,957
In view shining brightly.

25
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:36,860
Oh, who knows what's waiting for you.

26
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:40,117
Dream living, that's the way.

27
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,197
Make like a hurricane.

28
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:45,100
Now, got to make your mark today.

29
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:50,977
One dream, one wish.

30
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:52,997
Your dreams don't run away.

31
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,917
Go for the knockout.

32
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,080
Over the top!

33
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:24,830
Daddy!

34
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,920
It's not fair!

35
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:35,240
You can't die!

36
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:43,060
No one told us.

37
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:46,700
I thought smiles were just a
kind of man-made Devil Fruit.

38
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,580
Sir Yasui, no!

39
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:13,540
We weren't fast enough. What now?

40
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:16,239
Do you think they're going to riot?

41
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:31,317
You stood right before me.

42
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:32,317
And I didn't even know.

43
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:34,237
I failed you.

44
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:36,620
I should commit sepulchre.

45
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:40,640
Lord Yasui.

46
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:56,380
Don't know Yasuhu's gone!

47
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,520
Oh my lord, Yasuhu!

48
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:01,620
He was taken too soon!

49
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:06,837
Am I missing something here?

50
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:11,097
The people from Ebisu Town loved him
so much, why would they be laughing?

51
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:12,800
This doesn't make sense.

52
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:30,540
You're a sick bastard, Orji.

53
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:32,560
You must think this is funny.

54
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:47,877
Those poor chumps are crazy,

55
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:51,577
laughing their asses off at
the death of their old daimyo.

56
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:55,060
You are a bastard, Orochi!

57
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:03,617
I can scarcely believe it, sir,
Yasui—he was alive all these years?

58
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:09,740
years He knew about our strategy, and
he knew that the enemy had thwarted it.

59
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:12,440
Sir Yasui, I see now.

60
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:14,660
You let them seize you.

61
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:18,960
Your sacrifice has
given us another chance.

62
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:25,760
There must be some reason, right?

63
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:27,470
Huh?

64
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:30,260
It doesn't matter who it is.

65
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:33,565
Nobody deserves to be
laughed at when they die.

66
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:35,396
It's just not right.

67
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,480
This is due to the side
effects of the Smilefruits.

68
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:43,180
They are here as well.

69
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:46,604
People who can only laugh
even when they're sad.

70
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,240
You've been gone a while.

71
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:53,657
Have you seen this?

72
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:57,120
Do the words Smilefruit ring a bell?

73
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,560
That was my mistake.

74
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:02,800
I should have told you.

75
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:10,960
The smiles that the people of
Ebisu wear, they are merely masks.

76
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:18,460
Masks that they can never
remove till they're dead.

77
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:24,700
Kaido and Orochi began this
operation a few years ago.

78
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:30,197
They started importing some
kind of artificial fruit in

79
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:33,515
exchange for the weapons that
are made in this country.

80
00:06:34,220 --> 00:06:38,357
The smile fruits, when you
eat those wretched things,

81
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:43,137
you invite the hatred of the sea and
can no longer swim but in return you'll

82
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:47,157
gain the strength of a wild beast and
their fearsome appearance as well,

83
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:50,917
all that stuff checks
out with what we know a

84
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,797
while back we destroyed
the factory that made them.

85
00:06:53,880 --> 00:07:00,477
I know master keen did mention that but
their plan had gone on for quite some time!

86
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:02,080
The damage had been done.

87
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,792
A great number of fruits have
been brought to our country.

88
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:14,037
Kaido's objective was to
strengthen his ranks by giving

89
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:17,649
that beastly power to as many
of his underlings as possible.

90
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:21,520
He wanted the strongest pirate
crew the world had ever seen.

91
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:27,720
But there's always a catch when
something sounds too good to be true.

92
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:34,600
The success rate of that artificial
strength enhancer was only 10 percent.

93
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:40,840
So if 10 people ate one of those fruits,
only one of them would gain an ability.

94
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:53,137
The other nine would face the consequences
without gaining anything in return.

95
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:55,997
Of course, they won't
be able to swim anymore,

96
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:59,777
but the flawed chemical
mixture causes another effect.

97
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:05,097
Those who fail to inherit the power lose
their ability to express sorrow or anger;

98
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:07,517
all they can do is laugh.

99
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:11,217
What so the chemical
mixture she mentioned?

100
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:14,577
That must be the sad stuff that
Caesar was working on, right?

101
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:18,977
We knew it was bad news, but this
is pretty sick even for Caesar.

102
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:23,517
Kaido doesn't care; he'll
sacrifice as many minutes he must.

103
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:28,220
He just wants that power,
no matter the cost.

104
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:36,357
Kaido's crew is divided
into three categories;

105
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:39,340
the power of the fruit
determines your place.

106
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:43,077
Those who haven't eaten
one and are hoping for a

107
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:46,480
chance to gain a beast
power are called waiters.

108
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:51,957
The lucky members who beat the odds and

109
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:55,220
successfully gained the
power are the gifters.

110
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:01,577
And the unlucky ones who
ate the fruit and were left

111
00:09:01,660 --> 00:09:04,719
with nothing but endless
laughter are the pleasures.

112
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:08,650
However,

113
00:09:08,733 --> 00:09:12,917
it seems that Kaido and his twisted
associates found their condition amusing.

114
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,320
And so,

115
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:17,177
their creation was named
in mockery of the only

116
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:20,554
expression the pleasures were
capable of making anymore.

117
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:21,860
A smile.

118
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:30,760
It seemed odd to me,
calling the fruits that.

119
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,657
But I never thought it would
have such a cruel story.

120
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,340
Those guys really are evil.

121
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:38,780
The truth is, that's
not even the worst part.

122
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:45,117
Orochi came up with a
wicked plan when he noticed

123
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:47,965
most smile fruits were
discarded after a single

124
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:49,370
bite.

125
00:09:49,453 --> 00:09:53,744
They couldn't produce gifters, but they
still passed on the negative side effects.

126
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:57,937
So if he wanted to turn people into
pleasures out of cruelty, then he could...

127
00:09:58,020 --> 00:09:59,260
No.

128
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:01,717
Outside of the Capital, as you know,

129
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:05,737
is the town of leftovers, where people
were crying and dying of hunger.

130
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:08,937
Every day, Orochi was disgusted
by the sight of their suffering.

131
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:11,857
So he mixed in the
failed smile fruits with

132
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:13,457
the deliveries that came from the capital.

133
00:10:13,540 --> 00:10:16,140
Knowing full well how they would react.

134
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:23,120
So many apples, and they're still fresh.

135
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:26,997
This is a treat—let's share everyone!

136
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:27,910
everyone

137
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:42,401
Of course, after the first few times, they
knew exactly what they were getting into.

138
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:45,580
But what choice did they have?

139
00:10:46,860 --> 00:10:49,160
They were starving after all,

140
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:52,940
and their empty stomachs were
heedless to the consequences.

141
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:14,880
Thus Ebisertown was born,

142
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:19,880
a place of sickness and poverty
where everyone wears a smile, no

143
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:21,517
matter how they suffer.

144
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:26,417
The tragic place haunted by laughter,
where children can't even mourn?

145
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:28,088
the death of their parents.

146
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:36,060
So please,

147
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:39,960
don't blame them for laughing.

148
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:43,580
They're the ones hurting, most of all.

149
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:58,220
Of all the living creatures in the
world, Only a human can laugh, right?

150
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:00,800
Best of all, it's free.

151
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,904
So why waste a beautiful thing?

152
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:21,620
You can't die.

153
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,520
Please get up.

154
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,740
it's all his fault

155
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:40,660
he did this for the sake of cruelty

156
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:47,980
he robs them of all their joy then
robs them of their ability to breathe

157
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:54,900
it's too much if this isn't hell

158
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:56,960
That's what is

159
00:12:57,620 --> 00:12:59,800
What more can he take

160
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:10,000
Look at how happy they are to see you go,

161
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:16,277
Yasui A fitting aim You knew this
was my country How arrogant to

162
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:20,740
think that I would ever let you live
You're lucky you lasted so long,

163
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:24,620
H-Hog But now You're just a dead rat

164
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,360
And there you have it everybody,
your beloved old daimyo,

165
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:36,680
the famous Shimotsu
Kiyosui is lying face down,

166
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:39,517
dead in the dirt like the
miserable vermin he is!

167
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:43,840
Now laugh your asses off, because
we're all so happy to see him go!

168
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:50,557
This is the land of Wano,
a bright and joyful place!

169
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:54,040
Why, you might even mistake it for heaven!

170
00:13:59,620 --> 00:14:02,440
Keep laughing! More! More!

171
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:20,360
Where'd she go? Don't go!

172
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:33,820
You shouldn't be in there!

173
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:35,472
Please, Dock, come back!

174
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:36,810
Daddy!

175
00:14:39,860 --> 00:14:41,200
Don't leave me!

176
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:58,520
Please, Daddy!

177
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:02,000
Please, you have to get up!

178
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:06,580
Here, Daddy.

179
00:15:06,980 --> 00:15:09,380
I have some medicine that'll help you.

180
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:12,180
It's that girl!

181
00:15:12,420 --> 00:15:13,820
She came and ate Sabo!

182
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,160
It can't be!

183
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:16,630
Hey, wait!

184
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:19,640
You're saying she's
Tonoyasu's daughter? No way!

185
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,720
I'll bring you back. Don't worry.

186
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:26,560
This medicine here will heal any wound.

187
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:32,820
This toad oil works just like magic.

188
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:35,320
My friend who sells it told me so.

189
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:37,940
You'll be just fine.

190
00:15:43,180 --> 00:15:45,200
I'm sorry, Otoko.

191
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:49,437
It doesn't perform miracles at all.

192
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:50,700
I lied to you.

193
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:00,380
Come back!

194
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:16,057
What a lucky day?

195
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:17,780
Seems I found you.

196
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:26,060
Get out of my way!

197
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,480
Get out of my way!

198
00:16:29,820 --> 00:16:32,000
Get out of my way!

199
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:36,257
Get out of my way! Get

200
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:43,340
out

201
00:16:45,740 --> 00:16:46,570
of my way!

202
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:48,550
No!

203
00:16:48,633 --> 00:16:49,463
I should have known.

204
00:16:49,546 --> 00:16:52,940
You are Yasue's daughter as clear as day!

205
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:56,040
Who else could be so insolent?

206
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:58,280
You little rat!

207
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,000
You little shit!

208
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:02,140
It's all your fault!

209
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:06,500
If you hadn't laughed at
me like a damned fool,

210
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:09,500
then Komurasaki would
still be alive right now!

211
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:11,420
I'll kill you!

212
00:17:14,660 --> 00:17:19,780
You're wretched family has been
a pain in my ass for long enough.

213
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:29,580
Say goodbye.

214
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:36,980
Now die you little shit!

215
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:42,714
I'll lose you as well!

216
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:47,640
Finally, I'll have my revenge!

217
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:13,120
Oh, my God.

218
00:18:41,900 --> 00:18:43,640
I know those guys.

219
00:18:44,100 --> 00:18:48,420
It's Zorojuro the Magistrate
Killer and Sangoro the Sabo Cook.

220
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:56,440
Piss off.

221
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:58,040
Go figure.

222
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,477
Those two are always itching for a fight.

223
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:02,360
This is going to be a problem.

224
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:04,400
We can deal with it.

225
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:05,877
They did the right thing.

226
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:08,460
Yeah, I'm just glad Otoko is safe.

227
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:12,037
I've been looking forward
to this execution.

228
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,857
How dare you interrupt it!

229
00:19:13,940 --> 00:19:15,977
When the Shogun wants someone dead?

230
00:19:16,060 --> 00:19:17,080
You step aside!

231
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:20,737
Even if that brat wasn't Yasue's daughter.

232
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:23,600
She still committed an unforgivable crime.

233
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:25,697
Hey, samurai!

234
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:28,177
Kill all of that filthy rat's allies!

235
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:30,848
And anyone else who
tries to get in the way!

236
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:32,500
Yes, sir.

237
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:42,577
Uh-oh, those guys are
pointing right at us.

238
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:44,542
I'm thinking that we should run.

239
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:50,905
Scatter, you bunch of roaches!

240
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:52,350
Kill them!

241
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:11,725
Sorry, but I don't have
time for you right now.

242
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,740
I don't have time for you.

243
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:16,440
Then get out of my way, Browgoro.

244
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:18,457
Is that supposed to be a joke?

245
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:22,500
It's Sangoro, stupid, and you
stay out of my way, Masjuro.

246
00:20:23,620 --> 00:20:24,450
Masjuro?

247
00:20:24,533 --> 00:20:27,197
That's right, because your
head looks like a moss ball.

248
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,110
Does not!

249
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:31,840
I'll chop you to pieces right
along with Odorchi. Oh yeah?

250
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:35,037
Then I'll kick you to death
right along with Kaido.

251
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:36,100
You'll do what?

252
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:38,360
My daddy!

253
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:42,801
Otaku, thank goodness she's safe.

254
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:46,240
That man, could he be Zoro Juro's friend?

255
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:49,873
The swordman is definitely
Zoro, so that's one Straw Hat.

256
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:51,766
The other is Vince Mokesanji.

257
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:53,654
Strange wanted poster.

258
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:57,877
Perhaps all of the Straw Hats
are here in the land of Wano.

259
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:58,940
Not very subtle.

260
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:01,797
Defying the Shogun right
in the middle of town.

261
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:02,710
So what?

262
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:04,817
Who says we need to be subtle, huh?

263
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:05,730
Huh?

264
00:21:05,813 --> 00:21:07,100
I'll be as loud as I want.

265
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:12,260
Also, don't ever call me
a Vinsmoke again. Got it?

266
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:15,820
I'll make sure they leave
it off your gravestone.

267
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:22,720
Open fire.

268
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:28,680
Damn it.

269
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,059
We'll just have to keep at it then.

270
00:21:31,220 --> 00:21:32,050
Next row.

271
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:37,950
Fire!

272
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:45,940
Take Odako and run already, damn it!

273
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:47,820
No, not yet.

274
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:49,740
He needs to pay.

275
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:54,240
Those thugs really are
quite stubborn, aren't they?

276
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:58,480
Here, it's better if you
take her. Wait, what?

277
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:00,110
Why?

278
00:22:01,060 --> 00:22:02,280
He's looking at me.

279
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:04,180
Take him out! Hurry up!

280
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:08,217
I need all that ronin with bullets
before he tries to attack me!

281
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:09,540
I got this!

282
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:10,760
Run, Browgoro!

283
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:14,600
You bastard!

284
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:17,548
You have no right to
cut through my bullets!

285
00:22:17,700 --> 00:22:18,660
Sucker trap!

286
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:21,900
I won't be satisfied
till I end you myself!

287
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:23,000
Hey, Mosshead!

288
00:22:23,180 --> 00:22:25,097
You're not the one calling the shots!

289
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:26,280
Prepare to fire!

290
00:22:27,020 --> 00:22:27,880
Aw, crap.

291
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:29,270
No!

292
00:22:31,540 --> 00:22:33,220
We gotta get out of here!

293
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:35,280
Tonyasu gave his life.

294
00:22:35,500 --> 00:22:36,600
Don't waste that.

295
00:22:40,740 --> 00:22:41,570
Whoa.

296
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:42,860
One sec, mister.

297
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:45,457
I'm a firm believer in good old balance.

298
00:22:45,540 --> 00:22:48,360
Good and evil, black and
white, odds and evens.

299
00:22:48,920 --> 00:22:51,979
You really knocked him good,
so let's call it a day.

300
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:52,910
Yeah.

301
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:56,880
Let me tell you about our secret, okay?

302
00:22:57,260 --> 00:23:01,177
In this country, we have a name
for our trademark grin. You ready?

303
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:04,140
We proudly call it the Ebisu Smile!

304
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:06,277
It's where the place gets its name.

305
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:08,125
Poverty can't steal our smile.

306
00:23:09,460 --> 00:23:10,290
Yasuie.

307
00:23:14,180 --> 00:23:16,020
Why is he so strong?

308
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:19,127
Don't tell me the Akasaya
put him up to this!

309
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:21,000
Come on, useless samurai!

310
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:22,460
Protect me!

311
00:23:24,860 --> 00:23:26,800
720-caliber Phoenix!

312
00:23:39,680 --> 00:23:45,797
And who is that below that
is boss Kiyoshiro, my lord?

313
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:51,537
You are far too careless; the execution
site clearly lacks the security you require.

314
00:23:51,620 --> 00:23:56,957
That ronin truly is a menace—I
swear he was trying to murder me!

315
00:23:57,040 --> 00:24:02,777
Hey, Moss Head, what the
hell are you trying to pull?

316
00:24:02,860 --> 00:24:04,217
You're gonna get us all killed!

317
00:24:04,300 --> 00:24:05,130
Something

318
00:24:14,760 --> 00:24:16,557
so big—sneak up on me!

319
00:24:16,640 --> 00:24:17,470
on me

320
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:27,220
Fire on my signal.

321
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:32,440
What a busy day.

322
00:24:32,740 --> 00:24:34,420
Even more executions.

323
00:24:34,860 --> 00:24:35,840
So what now?

324
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:38,357
We can't just sit here
and watch this, right?

325
00:24:38,440 --> 00:24:39,600
It's getting ugly.

326
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:42,280
We gotta step in and throw down, bros.

327
00:24:42,380 --> 00:24:43,440
No, I object.

328
00:24:43,740 --> 00:24:46,681
We cannot afford to endanger
our plan any further.

329
00:24:47,120 --> 00:24:49,826
Also, we'll become
criminals if we fight them.

330
00:24:50,100 --> 00:24:52,277
Then we won't be able
to act in the capital.

331
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:57,060
Even so, I can't allow them to
put Lord Yasui's body on display.

332
00:24:57,520 --> 00:25:00,108
Preserving his honor
is the least we can do.

333
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:02,697
It's not that I disagree, but...

334
00:25:02,780 --> 00:25:04,200
Let's split up for now.

335
00:25:04,540 --> 00:25:06,637
Where should all of us
meet once things cool off?

336
00:25:06,720 --> 00:25:08,540
No, I'm staying here to fight.

337
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:10,100
It is far too soon.

338
00:25:10,320 --> 00:25:14,657
I cannot speak for the others, but Lord
Odin's allies must remain discreet for now.

339
00:25:14,740 --> 00:25:15,570
He's right.

340
00:25:15,653 --> 00:25:17,717
You two should keep a low profile and head

341
00:25:17,800 --> 00:25:20,437
out while the enemy is
still distracted but I,

342
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:24,317
our crew started this mess so
we'll take care of it, trust me.

343
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:25,937
We're used to this sort of thing.

344
00:25:26,020 --> 00:25:28,537
I am grateful.

345
00:25:28,620 --> 00:25:30,157
Let us depart.

346
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:32,937
We shall leave this in
their capable hands.

347
00:25:33,020 --> 00:25:38,920
Take the Shogun back to the castle.

348
00:25:41,300 --> 00:25:43,277
Don't stop until they're all dead!

349
00:25:43,360 --> 00:25:47,301
Every fool who opposes me must be
dealt with swiftly and violently!

350
00:25:48,500 --> 00:25:50,220
I'm not letting you go!

351
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:53,597
Kill him, Franky!

352
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:56,200
And he comes up!

353
00:26:01,100 --> 00:26:02,740
Is he good proof?

354
00:26:03,040 --> 00:26:04,860
But he's just a carpenter

355
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:09,900
All right, time! Can you dig it?

356
00:26:13,180 --> 00:26:14,460
Who are they?

357
00:26:14,860 --> 00:26:16,801
Where did these people come from?

358
00:26:17,780 --> 00:26:18,610
Huh?

359
00:26:18,693 --> 00:26:19,523
So there you are.

360
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:23,280
No, that guy stole Lord Yasui's body.

361
00:26:23,580 --> 00:26:25,877
What in the hell is
that guy planning to do?

362
00:26:25,960 --> 00:26:26,980
Don't you worry.

363
00:26:27,300 --> 00:26:29,535
We'll give your buddy a proper burial.

364
00:26:30,980 --> 00:26:31,810
Uh-oh!

365
00:26:34,180 --> 00:26:35,010
Huh?

366
00:26:35,093 --> 00:26:35,923
Who's that?

367
00:26:36,006 --> 00:26:36,900
Oh, hey!

368
00:26:37,100 --> 00:26:39,037
Should've known it was you, Usohachi!

369
00:26:39,120 --> 00:26:39,950
Nice save!

370
00:26:43,420 --> 00:26:45,540
Shoot that man on top of the ladder!

371
00:26:48,420 --> 00:26:49,440
Whoa, wait!

372
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:51,642
You guys can't snipe the sniper!

373
00:26:52,040 --> 00:26:53,477
That would be too ironic!

374
00:26:53,560 --> 00:26:58,300
Mellow Bellamy, Gigantesco
Narno, and Face!

375
00:27:01,420 --> 00:27:03,140
Thanks a ton, Oroby!

376
00:27:03,560 --> 00:27:06,031
Just how many allies do these people have?

377
00:27:06,400 --> 00:27:09,700
Wait a second, it's that
geisha from the castle.

378
00:27:09,980 --> 00:27:11,980
So she is a magic user.

379
00:27:12,260 --> 00:27:13,848
These are powerful enemies.

380
00:27:14,260 --> 00:27:15,180
Be careful!

381
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:19,600
Honami, leave them to me!

382
00:27:26,380 --> 00:27:27,860
Out of my way.

383
00:27:34,420 --> 00:27:36,360
Oh, I think not.

384
00:27:37,060 --> 00:27:38,120
Fine, then.

385
00:27:40,780 --> 00:27:42,220
I'll cut through!

386
00:27:52,940 --> 00:27:56,800
I am the Shogun's loyal dog.

387
00:27:58,540 --> 00:28:00,940
Hold up for you, Spector!

388
00:28:05,080 --> 00:28:06,660
Let's wrap this up quick.

389
00:28:06,980 --> 00:28:09,640
Sooner we leave, the better. Agreed.

390
00:28:09,860 --> 00:28:12,120
Special attack, godless combat.

391
00:28:13,380 --> 00:28:16,300
Leel's Lord, he can death for Marlowe!

392
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:20,220
Now, weapons left!

393
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:24,300
Tornado temple!

394
00:28:36,700 --> 00:28:39,797
Anyone nearby, we need aid!

395
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:43,160
A group of rebels are
rioting in Rasetsu Town.

396
00:28:43,600 --> 00:28:46,380
The Shogun said he wants
them dead or alive.

397
00:28:46,820 --> 00:28:48,980
Move in with the intent to kill!

398
00:28:49,700 --> 00:28:51,720
You got this! Go!

399
00:28:52,160 --> 00:28:54,000
Kick their asses!

400
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:56,040
Hell yeah! Mr.

401
00:28:56,220 --> 00:29:00,820
Straw Hat, those people showing on
the display, are they your crewmates?

402
00:29:01,480 --> 00:29:04,656
Guess I shouldn't cheer,
it's supposed to be a secret.

403
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:06,631
Well, it's probably okay.

404
00:29:08,780 --> 00:29:09,900
Beat him off!

405
00:29:10,140 --> 00:29:12,180
Yeah, nice! Like that! No!

406
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:14,310
Stop!

407
00:29:14,700 --> 00:29:16,237
Zorojuro! You can do it!

408
00:29:16,320 --> 00:29:17,520
Well, interesting.

409
00:29:18,020 --> 00:29:20,757
So that moss head dude is
your friend, Straw Hat?

410
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:23,620
That's the magistrate killer, Zorojuro.

411
00:29:23,820 --> 00:29:25,720
He must be part of your crew.

412
00:29:27,520 --> 00:29:28,700
I love it!

413
00:29:28,820 --> 00:29:31,937
This maniac thinks he can
get away with killing Orochi.

414
00:29:32,020 --> 00:29:32,850
Boo!

415
00:29:32,933 --> 00:29:34,317
Boo! Not now!

416
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:35,317
I'm busy!

417
00:29:35,400 --> 00:29:36,820
Read the room man.

418
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:41,297
This is good But sir a new
prisoner just arrived and he's

419
00:29:41,380 --> 00:29:45,160
a famous killer from the flower
capital Should I know him?

420
00:29:45,400 --> 00:29:47,297
Why don't you give me a hint, huh?

421
00:29:47,380 --> 00:29:48,857
Better to see him in person.

422
00:29:48,940 --> 00:29:51,400
I think He'll be coming through there

423
00:30:08,080 --> 00:30:09,880
He doesn't look like much.

424
00:30:10,120 --> 00:30:12,457
The Shogun lost patience with this piece

425
00:30:12,540 --> 00:30:15,140
of trash after failing
an important mission.

426
00:30:15,440 --> 00:30:20,360
Lord Oroji said he's worse than useless,
so you can punish him however you see fit.

427
00:30:25,760 --> 00:30:28,460
Head Kirikamazo, the famous killer.

428
00:30:28,840 --> 00:30:30,580
So that's who you are, huh?

429
00:30:30,840 --> 00:30:32,860
I've heard so much about you.

430
00:30:33,140 --> 00:30:34,280
And one more, sir.

431
00:30:42,660 --> 00:30:44,060
Okay, stop there!

432
00:30:44,420 --> 00:30:45,860
I've got some good news.

433
00:30:46,100 --> 00:30:48,757
We found him while we were
escorting Kamizo here.

434
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:51,720
And luckily, he wasn't too tough to catch.

435
00:30:52,060 --> 00:30:54,320
Captain Kidd is back where he belongs.

436
00:30:55,340 --> 00:30:56,380
It's Jaggy!

437
00:30:56,520 --> 00:30:57,760
He came to us.

438
00:30:57,980 --> 00:31:01,377
He was yelling something or other,
but I wasn't about to listen.

439
00:31:01,460 --> 00:31:04,017
Instead, I pulled out
my gun and shot him up.

440
00:31:04,100 --> 00:31:05,924
He didn't even try to run away.

441
00:31:06,120 --> 00:31:07,080
So here we are.

442
00:31:07,420 --> 00:31:11,420
Maybe he forgot he had those cuffs
on and still thought he was tough

443
00:31:12,780 --> 00:31:16,020
You dunce, that's almost cute kid

444
00:31:26,040 --> 00:31:28,357
Couldn't have been easy
to break out of here.

445
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:30,734
So why would he just surrender himself?

446
00:31:34,100 --> 00:31:35,400
Ha ha ha ha!

447
00:31:35,840 --> 00:31:36,700
Ha ha ha ha!

448
00:31:36,800 --> 00:31:38,200
Hey, stop it!

449
00:31:38,740 --> 00:31:39,570
Ha ha ha ha!

450
00:31:39,653 --> 00:31:40,640
Ha ha ha ha!

451
00:31:40,940 --> 00:31:42,740
Come on, dammit! I said stop!

452
00:31:44,100 --> 00:31:44,930
Ha ha!

453
00:31:45,100 --> 00:31:46,747
You always hated your laugh.

454
00:31:46,920 --> 00:31:47,860
This is wrong.

455
00:31:48,220 --> 00:31:49,660
This is messed up.

456
00:31:50,460 --> 00:31:52,280
You never laughed out loud.

457
00:31:52,580 --> 00:31:55,197
You couldn't stand to let
anyone hear it, right?

458
00:31:55,280 --> 00:31:58,877
And if someone out there was stupid
enough to make fun of your laugh,

459
00:31:58,960 --> 00:32:01,240
you'd beat the bastards half to death.

460
00:32:01,380 --> 00:32:03,200
Ha ha ha ha ha!

461
00:32:04,700 --> 00:32:05,780
Stop it.

462
00:32:06,020 --> 00:32:07,440
I'm begging you.

463
00:32:07,700 --> 00:32:12,465
You started wearing a mask because you
didn't even like to show your face, right?

464
00:32:12,780 --> 00:32:14,360
That's the man I knew.

465
00:32:15,380 --> 00:32:17,520
What the hell did they do to you?

466
00:32:18,020 --> 00:32:21,255
I've got no clue what happened
after we were separated.

467
00:32:21,480 --> 00:32:22,760
Did Kaido do this?

468
00:32:23,100 --> 00:32:25,760
Horichi, where's everyone else?

469
00:32:26,740 --> 00:32:28,020
Say something!

470
00:32:30,840 --> 00:32:32,960
Come on, turn around.

471
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:34,860
Why won't you answer me?

472
00:32:35,800 --> 00:32:36,630
KILLER!

473
00:32:40,320 --> 00:32:41,150
What?

474
00:32:41,233 --> 00:32:42,063
That's who he is?

475
00:32:48,140 --> 00:32:50,560
He's gotta be the guy he was with before.

476
00:32:51,280 --> 00:32:54,277
Jaggy must have got caught
when he tried to save him.

477
00:32:54,360 --> 00:32:56,460
He suffered a cruel fate.

478
00:32:56,740 --> 00:32:58,387
They gave him a smile fruit.

479
00:32:58,500 --> 00:33:03,400
Now all of his emotions are locked away,
hidden behind a mask of endless laughter.

480
00:33:03,700 --> 00:33:06,920
Oh, gee, you really are
a heartless monster.

481
00:33:15,040 --> 00:33:18,360
What in the hell did
those bastards do to you?

482
00:33:26,520 --> 00:33:27,920
How dare you?

483
00:33:28,120 --> 00:33:29,017
He's my partner!

484
00:33:29,100 --> 00:33:31,200
Whoever takes this won't pay!

485
00:33:33,100 --> 00:33:34,400
You sons of bitches!

486
00:33:34,680 --> 00:33:35,840
Where's everyone?

487
00:33:36,240 --> 00:33:37,620
Where's my crew?

488
00:33:57,520 --> 00:34:01,040
And that's why you don't screw with me!

489
00:34:02,120 --> 00:34:03,740
Let them go!

490
00:34:05,080 --> 00:34:07,980
Oh, I don't take orders
from you, Pipsqueak.

491
00:34:11,880 --> 00:34:16,860
By the way, I came up with a
little game to live things up.

492
00:34:32,640 --> 00:34:36,900
I kept you all waiting, but
the party's back on track now.

493
00:34:39,280 --> 00:34:42,260
Sumo Inferno, round two!

494
00:34:44,320 --> 00:34:46,480
No mercy this time.

495
00:34:53,640 --> 00:34:57,020
I've added a new rule to
spice things up a bit.

496
00:34:58,520 --> 00:35:01,177
You'll still be fighting
against countless opponents,

497
00:35:01,260 --> 00:35:03,717
and the spikes in your
collars will still kill you.

498
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:05,617
if you step outside of the ring.

499
00:35:05,700 --> 00:35:07,800
Don't worry, that hasn't changed.

500
00:35:08,360 --> 00:35:09,440
But now,

501
00:35:09,800 --> 00:35:11,517
as long as you're still alive,

502
00:35:11,600 --> 00:35:16,357
the runaway and his happy
little pal will be drowning

503
00:35:16,440 --> 00:35:21,817
in that tank there you
get it if you want them

504
00:35:21,900 --> 00:35:25,957
to come out of the water
you gotta lose your head

505
00:35:26,040 --> 00:35:31,017
you and the old man that's
stupid they're not my

506
00:35:31,100 --> 00:35:34,177
crew they have nothing to
do with me I don't care

507
00:35:34,260 --> 00:35:38,157
cuz you seem pretty angry
so even if you aren't crew

508
00:35:38,240 --> 00:35:42,157
mates they must mean
something to you it must be

509
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:45,181
because your rivals from
the same generation right

510
00:35:45,580 --> 00:35:48,357
well if you're such a kind and
charitable person you can die

511
00:35:48,440 --> 00:35:52,397
anytime and save them but i'd make
it quick if i were you a little

512
00:35:52,480 --> 00:35:57,777
water goes a long way even if
you're a famous pirate it only takes

513
00:35:57,860 --> 00:36:02,840
five centimeters to drown and no
one can hold their breath forever.

514
00:36:07,480 --> 00:36:09,960
Now let the games begin.

515
00:36:46,980 --> 00:36:48,220
You're a coward!

516
00:36:48,680 --> 00:36:51,240
Why don't you get in here and fight me?

517
00:36:53,040 --> 00:36:55,280
I'll kick your ass and settle this!

518
00:36:55,420 --> 00:36:57,120
I'm sick of your games!

519
00:37:07,240 --> 00:37:09,980
You're not the one calling the shots here.

520
00:37:10,560 --> 00:37:13,140
My house, my rules, kid.

521
00:37:13,540 --> 00:37:15,460
Now sit your ass down.

522
00:37:19,520 --> 00:37:20,350
Mr.

523
00:37:20,433 --> 00:37:21,280
Straw Hat, no!

524
00:37:27,860 --> 00:37:29,040
Listen, punk.

525
00:37:30,860 --> 00:37:32,480
You can't win.

526
00:37:36,320 --> 00:37:38,760
I don't see what makes you so hopeful.

527
00:37:44,840 --> 00:37:49,252
It was never possible for either of
you to make it out of this place alive.

528
00:37:50,100 --> 00:37:52,980
Hope isn't an option, only despair.

529
00:37:57,780 --> 00:38:00,540
This is an execution, you get that?

530
00:38:02,840 --> 00:38:04,760
You're all gonna die.

531
00:38:35,140 --> 00:38:37,417
You don't decide where I die?

532
00:38:37,500 --> 00:38:40,240
That's up to me.

533
00:39:05,260 --> 00:39:07,940
Hey, the hell was that?

534
00:39:12,040 --> 00:39:13,500
Did something happen?

535
00:39:14,240 --> 00:39:15,440
Somebody respond!

536
00:39:16,500 --> 00:39:19,720
Master Queen, we lost contact
with the guards outside!

537
00:39:53,880 --> 00:39:56,700
Finally, we made it.

538
00:40:00,380 --> 00:40:03,480
Now, where's my suit?
